Recent experimental data from $b 	o c$ decays have been used to make predictions about the rare decay of $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$, within the $U_1$ leptoquark model. Our calculations take into account constraints from $B_c 	o \pi 	au  ar{
u}$ decay and indicate that $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ branching ratio should be between $0.34 	imes 10^{-4}$ and $1.4 	imes 10^{-4}$, which can be compared to the current experimental range of $2.8 	imes 10^{-4}$ to $8.4 	imes 10^{-4}$.
